Z||000000||87ECO5||02-25-2000||09:37 PM||||OK, so this afternoon, my wife takes the kids up the street to Wal-mart to shop.  After parking the car, she randomly selects a shopping cart and puts the kids in it.  My oldest picks up a sheet of paper that was laying in the cart and hands it to her mother.  Here's what it said:<P><B>NHTSA</B><BR><B>Office of Defects Investigation</B><BR><B>Service Bulletins Database</B><P><B>Report Date:  January 4, 2000 06:50:16 PM</B><P>Service Bulletin Number:  87-6-GAS-44<BR>Bulletin Sequence Number:  091<BR>Date of Bulletin:  8706<BR>NHTSA Item Number:  91806<BR>Make:  PONTIAC<BR>Model:  FIERO<BR>Year:  1987<BR>Component:  ENGINE:  VALVES:  VALVE TRAIN<BR>Summary:  CYLINDER HEAD EXHAUST VALVE GUIDE NEAR-ENGINE EXHIBIT VALVE TRAIN NOISE MISSING AND ROUGH IDLE-REPLACE ALL FOUR EXHAUST VALVES WITH CORRECT OVERSIZE VALVES-IF OVERSIZE VALVES NOT AVAILABLE REPLACE CYLINDER HEAD AND ALL FOUR EXHAUST VALVES WITH STANDARD SIZE VALVES-ALL 1987 PONTIAC GRAND AM/FIERO AND 6000 MODELS WITH 2.5L L4 ENGINES (VIN CODES R AND U)<P><BR>Now, for those of you that participated in my previous thread <B>'Can you guess what this noise is'</B>, you'll know I was complaining about a noise that sounded like a dragging chain in the engine of my 1987 coupe with the 2.5L and that I was convinced it was the valve train!<P><B>TELL ME THIS WHOLE THING ISN'T ABSOLUTELY TOO WIERD!!!!!</B>  Spooky, don't you think?  Now, to replace the top end of my motor ...<p>[This message has been edited by 87ECO5 (edited 02-25-2000).]||||reg||4
